<title>EGYPT: Egypt March crude output down, natgas up - EGPC.</title>
<headline>Egypt March crude output down, natgas up - EGPC.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian crude oil production went down slightly in March to an average of 845,161 barrels per day (bpd) from 845,400 bpd in February, the state's Egyptian General Petroleum Corp (EGPC) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>But EGPC said natural gas output rose to 1.306 billion cubic feet a day from February's 1.303 billion cubic feet.</p>
<p>Condensates were higher again in March at 38,064 bpd from 36,100 bpd in February, while butane and propane output was marginally down at 31,935 from 32,500, EGPC said.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
